# Git guesses whether a file is text by sniffing its first few kilobytes, and
# it guessed wrong about assets/video/ri75-ph-kv70.mp4: that file contains no
# null byte early enough to look binary, so git recorded it as LF text. The
# commit itself was fine, but the next checkout on a machine with
# core.autocrlf=true would have rewritten every 0x0A in the stream to 0x0D 0x0A
# and handed the next person a video that will not play.
#
# Nothing here is text, so nothing here gets line-ending conversion.
*.mp4   binary
*.webm  binary
*.mov   binary
*.webp  binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
